This is server side of SIG handling in OpenBSD.
See ntdll sig for details on why it is done.
To tell what thread is the target tid in an array that is shared with the
process. The Array lives in the file `sig-{pid}` where pid is Windows process
id in hex format %04x.
All 64 slots hold signal/tid pairs. If the table stays full after retries,
the request is dropped without broadcasting.

Index: server/sig_openbsd.c
